==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Shibalien]]s (800%) spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Doge]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Shibalien]]s (800%) spawn, delay 0.07~0.67 seconds<sup>2f~20f</sup>.
**20 [[Shibalien]]s (1,200%) spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**20 [[Shibalien]]s (1,000%) spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
**30 [[Shibalien]]s (800%) spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[Doge Dark]] spawns as the boss.
*When the base reaches 70% HP:
**1 [[Gabriel]] spawns as the boss.
*When the base reaches 60% HP:
**1 [[Metal Doge]] spawns as the boss.

==Strategy==
With the beginning of the chapter 25 of the Stories of Legend, you should have the [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] from at least one chapter of [[Into the Future]], as [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] will start to appear as a threat.

First, stall the first Shibaliens, then build up a stack of attackers.

Doge will spawn, along with many more Shibaliens. While the Doge has an enormous strength magnification, it still isn't high enough to be consider him much of a threat. Just use a couple of midrange attackers such as [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] and he should die in seconds (all while meatshielding properly, of course). A similar process can then be repeated for every wave.

If you can get the second wave of Shibaliens just behind hitting range at the base then you can destroy the base without killing them which prevents the succeeding bosses from spawning, making you win the level.

Any strong [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion]] units make this stage an absolute pushover on 2-4 crowns.

==Trivia==
*Valkyrie Plains is the first [[Stories of Legend]] to have an [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemy.

